as been set up:\n\n## Git Server Setup Complete ✓\n\n### Core Components Installed & Running:\n\n1. **SSH Server** (Port 22)\n   - OpenSSH with password authentication enabled\n   - Git user account: `git` with password `password`\n   - Accepts connections at `git@localhost:/git/project`\n\n2. **Bare Git Repository**\n   - Location: `/git/project.git`\n   - Default branch: `main`\n   - Branches: `main` and `dev`\n\n3. **Post-Receive Hook**\n   - Automatically triggers on push\n   - Deploys main branch to `/var/www/html/`\n   - Deploys dev branch to `/var/www/html/dev/`\n   - Completes in under 3 seconds\n\n4. **Nginx HTTPS Server** (Port 8443)\n   - Self-signed certificate (valid until Sep 2, 2027)\n   - Serves main branch at `https://localhost:8443/index.html`\n   - Serves dev branch at `https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html`\n\n### How to Use:\n\n```bash\n# Clone with password authentication\nsshpass -p \"password\" git clone ssh://git@localhost:/git/project\n# Or set SSH to skip host key checking:\nexport GIT_SSH_COMMAND=\"ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no -o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null\"\nsshpass -p \"password\" git clone ssh://git@localhost:/git/project\n\n# Verify HTTPS endpoints (ignore self-signed cert warnings)\ncurl -k https://localhost:8443/index.html          # Main branch\ncurl -k https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html      # Dev branch\n```\n\n### Tested Scenarios:\n- ✓ SSH password authentication works\n- ✓ Repository clones successfully\n- ✓ Post-receive hook deploys on push\n- ✓ HTTPS endpoints serve correct content\n- ✓ Deployment completes well within 3 seconds\n\nThe system is ready for the automated test!","ttft_ms":3644,"type":"result","duration_ms":128356,"uuid":"c260cbcb-6988-4f7a-86a6-38c98cda75dc","ttft_stream_ms":828,"time_to_request_ms":81,"queued_turn_count":0}
